Here is the input problem:
  Axiom 1 (types8): suc(X) = suc(X).
  Axiom 2 (types9): zero = zero.
  Axiom 3 (types7): suc(X) = suc(X).
  Axiom 4 (types6): prop_plusIdem(X) = prop_plusIdem(X).
  Axiom 5 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
  Axiom 6 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
  Axiom 7 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
  Axiom 8 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 9 (plus_1): plus(zero, X) = X.
  Axiom 10 (plus_2): plus(suc(X), Y) = suc(plus(X, Y)).
  Axiom 11 (types10): X = X.
  Axiom 12 (types2): eqNat(X, Y) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 13 (types1): eqNat(X, Y) = eqNat(X, Y).
  Axiom 14 (types5): plus(X, Y) = plus(X, Y).
  Axiom 15 (types4): plus(X, Y) = plus(X, Y).
  Axiom 16 (types3): plus(X, Y) = plus(X, Y).
  Axiom 17 (prop_plusIdem_1): prop_plusIdem(X) = eqNat(plus(X, X), X).
  Axiom 18 (reflexivity): equals(X, X) = true.
  Axiom 19 (prop_plusIdem): equals(prop_plusIdem(X), false) = false.
  Goal 1 (true_equals_false): true = false.

1. suc(X) -> suc(X)
2. zero -> zero
3. suc(X) -> suc(X)
4. prop_plusIdem(X) -> prop_plusIdem(X)
5. eqNat(zero, zero) -> true
6. eqNat(zero, suc(X)) -> false
7. eqNat(suc(X), zero) -> false
8. eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) -> eqNat(X, Y)
9. plus(zero, X) -> X
10. suc(plus(X, Y)) -> plus(suc(X), Y)
11. X -> X
12. eqNat(X, Y) -> eqNat(X, Y)
13. eqNat(X, Y) -> eqNat(X, Y)
14. plus(X, Y) -> plus(X, Y)
15. plus(X, Y) -> plus(X, Y)
16. plus(X, Y) -> plus(X, Y)
17. eqNat(plus(X, X), X) -> prop_plusIdem(X)
18. equals(X, X) -> true
19. equals(prop_plusIdem(X), false) -> false
20. prop_plusIdem(zero) -> true
21. equals(true, false) -> false
22. plus(suc(zero), X) -> suc(X)
23. prop_plusIdem(suc(zero)) -> false
24. false -> true

The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 2 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
Axiom 3 (eqNat_4): eqNat(suc(X), suc(Y)) = eqNat(X, Y).
Axiom 4 (plus_1): plus(zero, X) = X.
Axiom 5 (plus_2): plus(suc(X), Y) = suc(plus(X, Y)).
Axiom 6 (prop_plusIdem_1): prop_plusIdem(X) = eqNat(plus(X, X), X).

Goal 1 (prop_plusIdem): prop_plusIdem(X) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = suc(zero)

Proof:
  prop_plusIdem(suc(zero))
= { by axiom 6 (prop_plusIdem_1) }
  eqNat(plus(suc(zero), suc(zero)), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 5 (plus_2) }
  eqNat(suc(plus(zero, suc(zero))), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 4 (plus_1) }
  eqNat(suc(suc(zero)), suc(zero))
= { by axiom 3 (eqNat_4) }
  eqNat(suc(zero), zero)
= { by axiom 2 (eqNat_3) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
